{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792436459,"nonce":"N9RSS3W6PJZW9ZyqhL2xgm25+20=","message":"Implemented in f0886c379e43f226e04fd5470497de79475f64f8, local, not pushed.\n\nKind::Canvas and Item::Canvas preserve kind 33 records between ordinary primitive runs, images and layers. Record::canvas validates the resource slot, geometry, display scale and finite rows, retains the producer's resource scale and shape payload, and reports malformed numeric records as CanvasData. Primitive-only decoding continues to report kind 33 as needing the ordered executor. The ABI schema and native painting are unchanged.\n\nThe approved callback API is Painter::set_canvas, remove_canvas and create_canvas_pipeline. CanvasPaint accepts synchronous closures or retained state implementations, with Send on native and no Send requirement on wasm. CanvasFrame borrows the device, queue, command encoder, current target, content size, full-frame logical affine, physical target origin and size, pixel ratio, resource scale and scissor. begin_pass loads the current layer and binds the prepared pipeline and frame group. Extra consumer groups start at 1. Shared WGSL helpers transform local vertices and apply the content box, screen/local/shaped clips, fades and record opacity to straight RGBA fragment output. Every custom fragment must call canvas_clip; a scissor alone is not exact. Custom vertex buffers and cached image textures are covered by the tests. Each draw is submitted before frame uniforms or auxiliary rows are reused for the next callback. missing_canvases reports missing canvas slots separately from the existing missing-image return value and clears at each render. Replacement/removal releases captured resources.\n\nCanvas callbacks do not allocate a canvas render target or force enclosing layers to the full frame. Frame data uses a retained 464-byte uniform buffer and a retained Rgba32Float auxiliary texture, initially 16 KiB and enlarged for polygon points; no shader storage is needed. Caller pipelines, buffers and optional cached images persist across frames. Existing layer effects and tight texture pooling remain in use; callbacks expose both the global transform and accumulated texture origin. A mutation forcing full-frame canvas layers is caught by the metadata assertions. These are implementation costs, not benchmark results.\n\nTwenty-eight fixtures, fourteen scenes at display scales 1 and 2, came from the unmodified blinc_abi a92f5c0 encoder. An independent CPU oracle evaluates raw-record clipping, procedural local colour, premultiplied paint-order compositing and nested layer colour matrices/opacity. On Apple M1 Pro, Metal, every canvas scene stays within 1/255 in all four channels. Coverage includes content padding and inherited opacity, transformed rounded screen clips, intersected fading bounds, ellipse/rounded-rectangle/polygon shape clips, even-odd and nonzero rings, independent shape/canvas transforms, bevel corners, consecutive clipped canvases, images and primitive runs around callbacks, cached texture binding, custom retained vertex buffers, positive layer origins, nested layers and callback replacement/removal/missing reports. The two layered polygon scenes omit four probes each at scale 2 using the existing 0.001 logical-pixel boundary guard; all other scenes omit none. The callback metadata also checks target texture dimensions remain smaller than the frame.\n\nMutations: dropping clips and record opacity fails by 165/255, removing inverse shape-frame translation into a layer fails by 100/255, and moving canvas records to the front of their paint list fails by 20/255. Expanding a canvas layer to the full frame preserves pixels but fails its target-origin/size assertions. All temporary mutations and capability overrides were restored. All 27 display-list GPU tests and the clip-fill-rule GPU test pass with normal capabilities. All 27 display-list tests also pass with vertex storage disabled. With both storage flags disabled and primitive/glyph capacities set to 1024, all 26 canvas-only render cases pass on Metal; the mixed primitive-order scene is excluded because ce34b20 still tracks stale SDF data-texture packing. Actual WebGL2, PowerVR/Adreno compilation and mobile pixels remain unverified.\n\nGate: fmt; workspace clippy with no new warnings; 1,900 workspace nextest tests passed, 53 skipped; docs with warnings denied; wasm and iOS compile checks; and threaded layout/CN tests pass. The canvas API doctest compiles. All 96 GPU-free integration tests and both canvas helper/resource-lifetime unit tests pass. The separate DSL run has 516 passed, 28 failed, 10 skipped, with exactly the same failing names as the untouched ff83adca baseline under a33d2b9. The test suite uses the same recursion limit as blinc_gpu to compile retained wgpu handles under the callback's Send bound without a compiler recursion warning. No dependency sources or shared ClipPath/CSS types changed.","files":null}]}